{
  "id": "Compound::DB00553 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Methoxsalen appears to interact with Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected pathways involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Methoxsalen binds to Cyp2a13, which then participates in metabolic processes that ultimately involve Cyp3a4. This is supported by multiple paths showing that Cyp2a13 is involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics and aromatase activity, both of which are linked to Cyp3a4. Additionally, Cyp2a13 is involved in oxidoreductase activities, which are also associated with Cyp3a4. These mechanisms imply that Methoxsalen may influence Cyp3a4 through the activation or modulation of Cyp2a13, which in turn affects the metabolic processing of xenobiotics and other substrates. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Methoxsalen in modulating Cyp3a4 activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
